          "settings": {
            "question": "What is honeydew honey?",
            "answer": "<p>Honey made from honeydew rather than flower nectar. Honeydew is a sweet sap that small insects leave on trees. Bees collect it, and the honey they make from it is darker and less sweet than blossom honey, with a resinous, almost malty taste.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does raw mean here?",
            "answer": "<p>It is not heated above hive temperature at any stage, it is not filtered and it is not blended with any other honey. Nothing is added to it.</p>"
